    {
      "id": "9up3327",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: DEFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Deflation is a sustained decrease in the general price level of goods and services, resulting in a negative inflation rate.",
        "Disinflation refers to a deceleration in the rate of inflation, where prices continue to rise but at a slower rate.",
        "Stagflation is a economic condition combining slow economic growth, high unemployment, and high inflation.",
        "Deflation increases the real value of debt, discouraging borrowing and consumer spending.",
        "RBI monetary measures and Government fiscal intervention are required to prevent a deflationary spiral and control stagflation."
      ],
      "id": "njmk6vj"
    },
