    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Crucial SSC distinction: Disinflation is NOT Deflation; during disinflation, prices are still rising, just at a lower percentage rate.",
        "Stagflation contradicts the classical Phillips Curve, which assumes an inverse relationship between inflation and unemployment.",
        "Deflationary spirals lead to reduced business profits, wage cuts, and rising unemployment."
      ],
      "id": "i9lyf8w"
